>
> Our next OP meeting will be *this* Wednesday on 9 November.
>
> Minutes from last month's OP call are archived at:
>
> ftp://ftp.pwg.org/pub/pwg/fsg/minutes/OP-Minutes-20111012.htm
>
> Agenda:
>
> (1) OP Logistics - Status of LF Infrastructure (Till Kamppeter)
>
> OpenPrinting web server is back: Automatic downloads and OpenPrinting DB
> web site work again, HPLIP plugin download works again, audio recordings
> of last two meetings are uploaded. BZR for Foomatic and CPD is not back
> yet (will be done this week).
>
> (2) Status of Common Printing Dialog (Lars Uebernickel)
>
> (3) Status of Mobile Print project (Glen Petrie)
>
> (4) PWG Highlights for Open Printing (Ira McDonald)
> - PWG meeting on 6-8 December at Dell in Austin, TX
>
> (5) Ubuntu Developer Summit (UDS) in Orlando
>
> - PostScript as standard print job format deprecated:
> http://www.openprinting.org/
> https://blueprints.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+spec/desktop-p-new-cups-filters-package
>
> https://www.linuxfoundation.org/collaborate/workgroups/openprinting/pdfasstandardprintjobformat
>
> - Ubuntu Precise will support Google Cloud Print, easily accessible for
> users via GNOME System Settings
> - Ubuntu One will support Google Cloud Print and HP ePrint
> - Ubuntu Precise will probably still use system-config-printer as
> GNOME's new tool is missing too many important features.
> - Common Print Dialog will come in Q. Q. (12.10).
> - Mirror of OpenPrinting at Canonical is in the works.
>
